    "abstractText": "After cryoballoon pulmonary vein isolation, acute gastric hypomotility progressed to phytobezoar formation. The admission CT had already shown a mottled intragastric mass with entrapped gas, initially interpreted as retained food; when post-ablation symptoms persist, clinicians should re-examine the original imaging before escalating therapy.",
